    "['isis enable [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name>', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `isis enable 1`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface <interface-name>\\nset protocols isis interface lo0.0\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. The first command enables IS-IS on the specified interface (replace `<interface-name>` with the actual interface name like `ge-1/0/0.0`)\\n2. The second command specifically enables IS-IS on the loopback interface\\n3. Juniper requires interface names to include the unit number (typically .0)\\n4. The IS-IS instance (1 in HUAWEI) isn't explicitly configured in Juniper as it defaults to a single instance\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name>'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface lo0.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `isis enable 1`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface <interface-name>\\nset protocols isis interface lo0.0\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. The first command enables IS-IS on the specified interface (replace `<interface-name>` with the actual interface name like `ge-1/0/0.0`)\\n2. The second command specifically enables IS-IS on the loopback interface\\n3. Juniper requires interface names to include the unit number (typically .0)\\n4. The IS-IS instance (1 in HUAWEI) isn't explicitly configured in Juniper as it defaults to a single instance\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface lo0.0'}]]": 1,
