    "['isis enable [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name> level 2', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `isis enable 1`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface <interface-name> level 2\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, you need to specify the interface name (e.g., `ge-0/0/0`, `lo0`) when configuring IS-IS on an interface. The `level 2` corresponds to HUAWEI's `is-level level-2` configuration in the IS-IS process.\\n\\nFor a more precise translation that matches the original intent (enabling IS-IS process 1 on an interface), you might alternatively use:\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface <interface-name>\\n##\\n\\nThis simpler form would be sufficient if the IS-IS level is already defined globally in the Juniper configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name> level 2'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name>', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `isis enable 1`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface <interface-name> level 2\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, you need to specify the interface name (e.g., `ge-0/0/0`, `lo0`) when configuring IS-IS on an interface. The `level 2` corresponds to HUAWEI's `is-level level-2` configuration in the IS-IS process.\\n\\nFor a more precise translation that matches the original intent (enabling IS-IS process 1 on an interface), you might alternatively use:\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface <interface-name>\\n##\\n\\nThis simpler form would be sufficient if the IS-IS level is already defined globally in the Juniper configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name>'}]]": 1,
    "['isis enable [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface lo0.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols isis interface lo0.0\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/1.0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, enabling IS-IS on an interface is done per interface basis under `protocols isis`\\n2. The `.0` suffix indicates the logical unit number (default for Juniper interfaces)\\n3. The command is applied to all interfaces that had `isis enable 1` in the Huawei config (Loopback0, GE1/0/0, and GE1/0/1)\\n4. Juniper doesn't require the IS-IS process number (1) in the interface configuration since it's handled at the protocol level\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface lo0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols isis interface lo0.0\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/1.0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, enabling IS-IS on an interface is done per interface basis under `protocols isis`\\n2. The `.0` suffix indicates the logical unit number (default for Juniper interfaces)\\n3. The command is applied to all interfaces that had `isis enable 1` in the Huawei config (Loopback0, GE1/0/0, and GE1/0/1)\\n4. Juniper doesn't require the IS-IS process number (1) in the interface configuration since it's handled at the protocol level\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/1.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols isis interface lo0.0\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/0.0\\nset protocols isis interface ge-1/0/1.0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. In Juniper, enabling IS-IS on an interface is done per interface basis under `protocols isis`\\n2. The `.0` suffix indicates the logical unit number (default for Juniper interfaces)\\n3. The command is applied to all interfaces that had `isis enable 1` in the Huawei config (Loopback0, GE1/0/0, and GE1/0/1)\\n4. Juniper doesn't require the IS-IS process number (1) in the interface configuration since it's handled at the protocol level\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface ge-1/0/1.0'}]]": 1
